From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tariq Bashir <tbashir@brightsign.biz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:09:49 +0100
Subject: fix(input): report touch-generated click as mouse OS-22164

WebMouseEvent instances created from a WebGestureEvent default to pointer
type `mouse`. During touch tap handling, GestureManager subsequently replaced
that default with WebGestureEvent::primary_pointer_type before dispatching the
synthetic click.

On Wayland, Ozone receives external touchscreen input through the standard
wl_touch protocol and creates TouchEvents with EventPointerType::kTouch.
The gesture pipeline preserves that classification, so the replacement caused
the compatibility click to surface to JavaScript as a PointerEvent with
pointerType `touch`.

Do not overwrite fake_mouse_up.pointer_type when dispatching the synthetic
click. The event now retains WebMouseEvent's default `mouse` pointer type,
matching the behavior observed on macOS for this click path.

This is intentionally localized to the compatibility click dispatch. Changing
Ozone Wayland's wl_touch classification would relabel all touchscreen contact
events as mouse, affecting pointerdown, pointermove, pointerup, touch
semantics, multi-touch handling, gesture recognition, stylus handling, and
every Wayland touchscreen rather than only the JS click compatibility event.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/input/gesture_manager.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/input/gesture_manager.cc
index d6dd7e4d3d3623e08da98b18d349f0857c5b7990..dff51268e52fdf142572c31473237ef21c717713 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/input/gesture_manager.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/input/gesture_manager.cc
@@ -338,7 +338,11 @@ WebInputEventResult GestureManager::HandleGestureTap(
           *tapped_element, event_handling_util::ParentForClickEvent);
       auto* click_target_element = DynamicTo<Element>(click_target_node);
       fake_mouse_up.id = GetPointerIdFromWebGestureEvent(gesture_event);
+      // Brightsign disabling setting the pointer type for fake mouse up events
+      // this will keep the type as default, which is mouse
+#if 0
       fake_mouse_up.pointer_type = gesture_event.primary_pointer_type;
+#endif
       click_event_result =
           mouse_event_manager_->SetMousePositionAndDispatchMouseEvent(
               click_target_element, event_type_names::kClick, fake_mouse_up);
